## Declared substitutions
1. No DESeq2/R → hand-rolled DESeq2-equivalent in numpy: median-of-ratios size factors, NB2 GLM (log link,
   IRLS), gene-wise dispersion by standard method of moments, binned log-log dispersion trend, shrinkage with
   `df_prior=1`, Wald test on the condition coefficient. Size factors and dispersion medians/IQRs are in
   `results/qc_log.txt` and `results/model_report.json`.
2. No gseapy → hand-rolled hypergeometric (Fisher greater) + BH (approved substitute), `enrich_core.py`.

## Fixed decisions (pre-registered, unchanged)
Universe GENCODE v31 protein_coding, `count>=5 in >=7` samples → 14,358 genes (after dropping 18 `_PAR_Y`
copies and 4 residual duplicate symbols, logged); symbols = GENCODE `gene_name` (HGNC Approved used only as
cross-check: 14,185/14,358 present, 98.97% symbol agreement, 173 unmapped-to-HGNC kept via GENCODE);
primary design `~ sex + condition`, sensitivity `~ condition`; sets FDR<0.05 & |log2FC|>=0.585 (primary)
and >=1 (secondary), up/down/union; headline rule = min BH-adjusted p, ties by OR then gene count.

## Inputs / traps caught
`featureCounts` table is **space-padded, not tab-delimited** (`sep='\t'` silently yields 1 column);
60,662 genes × 17 cols. Counts contain **16** samples but coldata only **14** → MGD1640F, MGD1641F dropped.
coldata: disease 7 / control 7, sex F 10 / M 4, cross-tab disease 6F/1M vs control 4F/3M → confounded.

## Results actually obtained
| model | FDR<0.05 | FDR<0.05 & \|lfc\|>=0.585 | \|lfc\|>=1 |
|---|---|---|---|
| primary `~sex+condition` | 250 (189 up / 61 down) | **216 (169 up / 47 down)** | 172 (133 up / 39 down) |
| sensitivity `~condition` | 386 (268/118) | 294 (224/70) | 223 (165/58) |

Model agreement: Pearson r(log2FC)=0.951, Spearman 0.940; primary vs sensitivity set Jaccard 0.584 (188 shared).
QC: XIST 333.6 (F) vs 0.04 (M) CPM, DDX3Y 0.00 vs 81.1, RPS4Y1 0.01 vs 122.8 → sex labels reliable.
ASXL1 (sanity check of the filename-based label assumption, NOT proof of genotype):
primary log2FC = -0.045 (p=0.71, FDR=0.97), sensitivity log2FC = -0.106 (p=0.38, FDR=0.80), baseMean 3637,
CPM disease 88.2 vs control 94.5 → no expression difference, fully compatible with point-truncating mutation,
so the label assumption is neither confirmed nor refuted by expression.

## Validation of the substitution (validation_report.json / validation_log.txt)
200→60 label permutations of condition (sex kept, every 5th gene, 2,872 genes): null genes at FDR<0.05
mean 2.98, median 0, **max 69**; observed 250/14,358 with true labels. Null p-value histogram counts
[376, 334, 308, 290, 275, 268, 260, 257, 251, 253] per bin vs 287 expected → mild excess of small p-values,
i.e. the hand-rolled GLM is **slightly anti-conservative**; the true DE count is likely below 250 and the
lists should be read as candidate sets. PCA: PC1 (30.1%) unrelated to condition (p=0.90); condition signal
sits on PC2 (p=0.010)/PC3 — consistent with a weak effect against large inter-line variability.
The GO engine was unit-tested on **synthetic** annotation (planted term recovered at rank 1/41); it was
never run on real data because no annotation exists.

## Limitations
N=7v7 with 4 males total and 6F/1M vs 4F/3M confounding → low power, unstable sex adjustment; primary and
sensitivity sets differ by 78 genes (Jaccard 0.58), so any downstream top term could differ by model — that
is why both gene lists are delivered. GENCODE v31 / HGNC 2019-05 vs a current GO release would additionally
drop renamed symbols from the background. Thresholds were fixed before any enrichment and were not retuned.

## Unblocking (one line)
Drop any `goa_human.gaf(.gz)` or `gene2go` into `/workspace/data/` and run `python3 run_enrichment.py`
(or grant network + rerun `run_all.sh`); it fetches, parses, tests and ranks without further edits.
